# Clock table v1 (see patches/clock_v1/clock_v1.md). Row 21 of the
# module 0 clock table at 0x03079824: fields +4..+27 only (word 0 untouched).
name: clock-v1-row-21
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x3079a74
gate: build refuses unless the 24 stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: DSD-DFF: B core/bus kept at stock (480 MHz). Rockchip's RKNanoD
  SDK clocks this decoder class at 260 to 400 MHz (PowerManager.c,
  FREQ_EHOGG / FREQ_HAPE / FREQ_HALAC / FREQ_DSDIFF / FREQ_DSF), above
  the 240/288 v1 first wrote, and the decode load is unmeasured. A
  fields zeroed so the solver's row-1 floor parks A outputs at 96 MHz
  (the SDK runs the system core at 80 MHz for this class); PLL word
  carried over unchanged. Data-only edit; reversible by rebuilding
  from stock without this patch.
expect: 00389c1c00c2eb0b00c2eb0b00b4c40400389c1c00389c1c
replace: 00389c1c00000000000000000000000000389c1c00389c1c
